(o.o) 3 files · owasp-top10 · 0.12s
2 findings (1 high, 1 medium)

------------------------------------------------------------------------
HIGH  likely  Stack trace leaked in error response  A05:2021
------------------------------------------------------------------------
 src/users/users.controller.ts:14:16

  12 |       throw new InternalServerErrorException({
  13 |         message: 'could not load users',
  14 |         stack: err.stack,
     |                ~~~~~~~~~ leaks internal stack trace to the client
  15 |       })
  16 |     }

 -> fix (NestJS)   Throw the exception without a custom body; let the
                   built-in filter shape the response.
                   this.logger.error(err)
                   throw new InternalServerErrorException()
 -> why            Stack traces expose absolute file paths, dependency
                   versions, and internal call structure — enough to
                   fingerprint the stack and locate other weaknesses.
 i  ref            OWASP A05:2021 | CWE-209 | RULES.md#stack-trace-leak

------------------------------------------------------------------------
MEDIUM  possible  Security headers are not configured  A05:2021
------------------------------------------------------------------------
 src/main.ts:8:21

   6 | 
   7 | async function bootstrap() {
   8 |   const app = await NestFactory.create(AppModule)
     |                     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ no security headers configured here
   9 |   await app.listen(3000)
  10 | }

 -> fix (NestJS)   Register helmet in the bootstrap; it sets all of
                   these.
                   import helmet from 'helmet'
                   
                   const app = await NestFactory.create(AppModule)
                   app.use(helmet())
 -> why            Without these headers the browser enforces nothing:
                   strict-transport-security forces HTTPS for future
                   requests; content-security-policy limits which
                   scripts and origins the page may load;
                   x-content-type-options stops browsers guessing a
                   response's content type; x-frame-options blocks
                   clickjacking via framing; referrer-policy stops URLs
                   leaking to third parties.
 i  ref            OWASP A05:2021 | CWE-693 |
                   RULES.md#security-headers-missing

Run `owlwarden explain stack-trace-leak` for the full write-up.
